  "cityLand": true,
  "city": {
    "about": "Buildings from OpenStreetMap as 3 m voxels on an unturned grid (Venice has no street grid); a building with no height or levels is 13 m. water: the land is OSM's islands less the canals, paved in trachyte with white stone along the quays, and the canals' centrelines are written for the boats. The Campanile and the Salute are hand-built (src/shared/env/venetianLandmarks.ts), so their footprints are left empty; the Basilica, the Doge's Palace and San Giorgio keep their voxels, coloured and raised here",
